# ADR-037 generated-artifact watch refusal — CONSUMER POLICY.
#
# A claim watching a generated artifact is a tripwire on an output: it
# stales whenever the generator runs, and its evidence describes something
# nobody edits. Paths listed here are refused as watches (overridable with
# --generated-ok "<basis>", which then decays on the ADR-032 clock).
#
# THIS FILE IS DELIBERATELY EMPTY, and empty is a statement, not an
# omission: nothing in this repository is generated. Every tracked file is
# hand-authored except .truth/claims.jsonl, which the CLI already excludes
# structurally. An ABSENT file leaves the check dark and voices an advisory
# on every filing; an empty one arms it and says so out loud.
#
# Committed 2026-08-01 alongside .truth/citation-scope, for the same
# reason: a coverage audit found two ADR-shipped gates reporting nothing
# because their policy file had never been written. A gate that looks armed
# and checks nothing is worse than no gate.
#
# Add a path here the day this repo generates one.
#
# F3.1: the machine-readable form of the statement above. The prose
# said it since 2026-08-01 and nothing could check that it had been
# said at all -- an unattested empty file is byte-identical to the
# untouched default, so `doctor` now refuses to read one as policy.
